	zone = "The Hinterlands",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "zone" },
		{ type = "map" },
	},
	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Hinterlands are a wild country of green hills, deep forests and high cliffs that lies north-east of the {link:arathi-highlands}Arathi Highlands{/link} and east of the {link:hillsbrad-foothills}Hillsbrad Foothills{/link}. Few roads cross them, and fewer farms. For thousands of years they have belonged to the forest {link:trolls}trolls{/link}, whose temples and stepped cities still crown the hills. On a crag in the far west stands {link:aerie-peak}Aerie Peak{/link}, the home of the {red:wildhammer-clan}Wildhammer{/red} dwarves and their gryphons. In the far south-east, by the sea, the {link:revantusk-village}Revantusk{/link} trolls keep a village for the {link:horde}Horde{/link}. Between them lies a land at war with itself: three troll tribes who share nothing but their blood, a lodge of {link:high-elves}high elves{/link} far from home, and in the north-east a great tree where the green dragonkin keep watch.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records when the first trolls built in these hills. What is known is that the forests of the north were once part of the Amani empire, the realm of the forest trolls, and that the Amani never forgave the {link:high-elves}elves{/link} who settled the lands beyond. The ruined cities of the Hinterlands are troll work, and their altars are older than any human kingdom. The dwarves came much later. After the War of the Three Hammers, the Wildhammer clan left the defiled halls of {link:grim-batol}Grim Batol{/link} and made a new home at {link:aerie-peak}Aerie Peak{/link}. There, in the high country of the trolls, they tamed the wild gryphons and learned to fly.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The Hinterlands have no single master. The Wildhammers hold {link:aerie-peak}Aerie Peak{/link} under their High Thane, {link:falstad-wildhammer}Falstad Wildhammer{/link}. They are allies of {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} by blood, but they insist that they are no part of the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} and that friendship with them must be earned by deeds. The {link:revantusk-village}Revantusk{/link} trolls hold their village on the eastern shore in the name of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}, and they hate the Wildhammers bitterly. The {red:vilebranch-trolls}Vilebranch{/red} rule the south and the north-east from their temples. They eat the flesh of other trolls and offer captives to the blood god {link:hakkar}Hakkar{/link}. The {link:witherbark-trolls}Witherbark{/link} hold the south-west, where they serve a spider god of their own. The oozes of the old Horde camp at {link:skulk-rock}Skulk Rock{/link} have spread through the river valleys, and wolves, owlbeasts and wild gryphons hunt everything that moves.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The Wildhammer dwarves.{/b} They live at {link:aerie-peak}Aerie Peak{/link} with their gryphons. They are proud, loud and fiercely independent, and they remember old wrongs longer than their cousins in {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}.
• {b}The {link:revantusk-village}Revantusk{/link} trolls.{/b} Forest trolls of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}, they keep a village by the sea and fight the Vilebranch without mercy.
• {b}The Vilebranch trolls.{/b} The largest and most savage tribe of the land. Their capital is {link:jintha-alor}Jintha'Alor{/link}, where their priestess prepares sacrifices to {link:hakkar}Hakkar{/link}.
• {b}The {link:witherbark-trolls}Witherbark trolls{/link}.{/b} They dwell in the south-western villages and at {link:shadra-alor}Shadra'Alor{/link}. They once fought beside the Horde, and then they turned on it.
• {b}The high elves of {link:quel-danil-lodge}Quel'Danil{/link}.{/b} Rangers and scouts of the Highvale hold a hunting lodge in the west, near the dwarves.
• {b}The green dragonkin.{/b} At {link:seradane}Seradane{/link} in the north-east, dragonspawn and drakes guard a great tree and suffer no one to come near.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Amani Age.{/b} In ages past the forest trolls ruled these hills as part of a great empire. The {link:troll-wars}Troll Wars{/link} broke their power, but the trolls never left.
• {b}The Three Hammers.{/b} After the war of the three clans, the Wildhammers abandoned {link:grim-batol}Grim Batol{/link} and settled at {link:aerie-peak}Aerie Peak{/link}. They became the gryphon riders of the north.
• {b}The {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.{/b} When the orcish {link:horde}Horde{/link} marched north, the Amani trolls under {red:zul-jin}Zul'jin{/red} joined it in the hope of burning {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link}. The Wildhammers flew for the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} against them. The Horde held positions in the Hinterlands for a time, among them the camp at {link:skulk-rock}Skulk Rock{/link}. In the end it abandoned them.
• {b}The New Horde.{/b} Under {link:thrall}Thrall{/link}, the Horde found friends among the forest trolls again. The {link:revantusk-village}Revantusk{/link} joined it. The {link:witherbark-trolls}Witherbark{/link} first fought beside it and then betrayed it, and the {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear{/link} have sent grim messages north in return.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} Now the Revantusk wait for Zul'jin to return, the Vilebranch feed their {link:hakkar}blood god{/link}, and the dwarves of Aerie Peak count every gryphon they lose.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Hills",
			text = [=[• The {link:revantusk-village}Revantusk{/link} say that the three troll tribes of the Hinterlands have only two things in common: they are trolls, and they live in the Hinterlands.
• At {link:aerie-peak}Aerie Peak{/link}, a newcomer who calls the Wildhammers "{link:alliance}Alliance{/link}" will be corrected, loudly and at once.
• An old riddle, found far away on the shores of {link:stranglethorn-vale}Stranglethorn{/link}, speaks of a treasure hidden beneath the water at the foot of the great falls on the Hinterlands coast.
• A drunken gryphon rider of Aerie Peak once fell from his mount into the drowned temple of the Atal'ai in the {link:swamp-of-sorrows}Swamp of Sorrows{/link}, and lived to tell the tale for the price of a drink.]=],
		},
	},
})

